{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-tannaka-dual","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:tannaka-dual","kind":"definition","title":"Tannaka dual (emergent gauge group)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe"],"cites":["references/saavedra-rivano1972","references/deligne1990"],"tags":["category-theory","tannaka-krein","gauge-group","fibre-functor"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.TannakaDual","text":"tannaka-dual.md","leanSource":"tannaka-dual.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:tannaka-dual\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau \\colon \\mathbf{C} \\to R\\text{-}\\mathrm{Mod}</code> be the fibre functor. A symmetry is a family of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module automorphisms compatible with the tensor product — a monoidal natural automorphism of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code>. The <strong>Tannaka dual</strong>, or emergent gauge group,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  G \\;=\\; \\mathrm{Aut}^{\\otimes}(\\tau)</code></pre>\n<p>collects these families.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/tannaka-dual.md","heading":"Definition","number":"3.4.9","page":"b/def-tannaka-dual","qa":{"counts":{"pass":71,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.TannakaDual","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/tannaka-dual.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
